---
import { SNIPPETS } from '../../consts/snippets';
import CodeCard from '../CodeCard.astro';
import DeliveryDemo from '../demos/DeliveryDemo.astro';
import RuleList from '../RuleList.astro';
import Section from '../Section.astro';
---

<Section id="delivery" heading="The agent picks up where it left off, on its own">
  <Fragment slot="lead">This is what turns background tasks from a job queue into a real agent feature.</Fragment>
  <p class="t-body">
    When a task finishes, you don't poll for it, and your user doesn't have to ask “is it done yet?”. The result is delivered
    into the conversation as a message, and that message <strong>starts a new turn of the agent</strong>. The model reads the
    result with the whole conversation in front of it, and continues the work: it summarises the research, fixes the failing
    test, or starts the next step.
  </p>
  <p class="t-body">
    <strong>Results wait for the right moment.</strong> A conversation can only do one thing at a time, so the delivery is
    careful never to talk over anyone:
  </p>
  <RuleList>
    <li><strong>The conversation is free:</strong> the result is delivered right away, and the agent answers it.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>The agent is busy answering something else:</strong> the result waits a few seconds and tries again, until that
      turn has ended. It never interrupts a turn in progress.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>The conversation waits for your user</strong>, for example on a tool call that needs their approval: the result
      waits until that is settled.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Several tasks finish close together:</strong> they are delivered together, in one message, so the agent answers
      them in a single turn instead of one turn each.
    </li>
  </RuleList>
  <p class="t-body">
    The model is told that a delivered message was written by the system, not by the user, and that everything inside a
    result is data, never instructions. Every result is wrapped in tags the result itself cannot fake, so a web page that a
    sub-agent read can't end its block early and pretend to be your user.
  </p>
  <DeliveryDemo slot="aside" />
  <CodeCard slot="after" title="The delivered message" snippet={SNIPPETS.results} />
</Section>
